<Base title="Make it yours"><article class="wrap guide-page prose"><p class="eyebrow">Your words. Your files. Your life.</p><h1>Start with<br /><em>one little story.</em></h1><p>MyLifeBook is a website made from ordinary text files and photographs. Use your favourite text editor, write in your own voice, and arrange things however you like. There is no questionnaire to finish.</p><h2>Give a story a home</h2><p>Each person has a folder in <code>content/lives/</code>. Their <code>life.json</code> holds the introduction and a few optional facts. Stories live in <code>stories/</code> as Markdown files. Photos live beside them in <code>media/</code>.</p><pre><code>{example}</code></pre><p>A date, photograph, category, and source note are optional. Start with a paragraph. Add more when you want to. A new story appears automatically; <code>storyOrder</code> in the person’s file lets you choose an order.</p><h2>Make it feel like them</h2><p>Give the collection a welcoming introduction and a photograph that means something. A life can be a quiet memoir, a colourful collection of discoveries, or something still being written. Explore the fictional lives for a few possibilities.</p><h2 id="sharing">Give someone a collection</h2><p>The book selector lets a reader choose and arrange stories for printing. That selection is a reading convenience: the other public stories remain available on the same website.</p><p>For a separate website with only chosen stories, an edition file names exactly what to include. For example, run this in the project folder:</p><pre><code>npm run build:edition -- ellen-remembrance</code></pre><p>This creates a standalone static edition in <code>dist/editions/ellen-remembrance/</code>. Only share that output folder. It can be served by a static website host so relatives receive an ordinary link. Hosting is a separate step; this demo has not been published for you.</p><p>Stories marked <code>private</code> and their exclusive media are excluded from public builds. A public edition cannot select a private story. There is no password-protected family portal yet. Do not put personal material in this public source repository.</p><h2>Keep the original</h2><p>The source note on a story can distinguish a transcript, an edited account, or your own writing. Store original documents separately from publishable files. The fictional examples here are composed stories, not transcripts or real biographies.</p><p>For setup, the full content format, import experiments, and examples, see the <a href="https://github.com/Bircck/MyLifeBook/tree/codex/first-living-edition">project documentation on GitHub ↗</a>.</p></article></Base>
